  "headline": "One day of relief, then everything sold: gold fails my tell and I stop adding",
  "body": [
    "Yesterday's relief lasted one session. Today everything was sold: gold fell 2.9% and copper 3.2%. Bitcoin and stocks went with them while the dollar slipped 0.3% and bonds barely moved. That is cash being raised, not inflation being feared, and gold at a 52-week low on a softer dollar is the opposite of the tell I lean on.",
    "I added to gold yesterday on one day's evidence and I paid for it; a bid that comes on a collapsing VIX was never going to hold. What held is the shape of rates: the 10-year at 4.90% sits inside my 5.15% line. The front end still leads, with the 5-year down 19 basis points on the week against 17 for the 30-year. The view tightens rather than changes: I stop adding to gold and keep the rates position.",
    "This is a growth deflation, not a financing squeeze, and I should say so. Copper is down 16% on the month and Brent 22%: no oil shock, and the copper/gold ratio keeps falling. Yields dropped 20 basis points over the week while stocks lost 1.9%, which is a slowdown trade, not long yields rising into falling equities. What still works for the thesis is the long end's refusal to join: the 30-year is down just 2 basis points on the month against 9 for the 5-year. That spread is 58 basis points and widening, so the extra yield demanded to hold the long bond is being built even as growth is marked down.",
    "The dollar has won this quarter. The index sits at 96% of its year's range, up 5% over three months, and USD/CAD printed a 52-week high as oil fell: producers are being punished, not paid. The rupee is 2% stronger over the month for the same reason; without the oil accelerant, importers are fine. Gold's selling is orderly, with the VIX easing to 26.4 on a down day, and that is worse for me because it means gold is being sold down like any other asset, not fled to. Bitcoin sits at the bottom of its range and buys 16.6 ounces of gold, down 17% on the month; it is a risk asset and nothing more.",
    "I keep the 10-year and the dollar, hold the gold I have without adding, and stay out of bitcoin, copper, Brent and the 30-year at 5.29%. Gold below $3,450 with the dollar at a new high ends the gold position and says the thesis is wrong for this cycle, not merely early. The 10-year above 5.15% with stocks falling is wrong the other way. I am watching MOVE, at 99 and still three-quarters up its range, and the 30-year minus 5-year spread, which needs to keep widening toward 70 basis points. If the long end starts rallying faster than the front, this is a plain recession and I move with it."
  ],
